{"excerpt": "SHIP RECYCLING - Maritime Facts and Figures - Maritime Knowledge Centre (MKC) at International Maritime Organization Skip to Main Content International Maritime Organization Maritime Knowledge Centre (MKC) Maritime Facts and Figures SHIP RECYCLING Search this Guide Search Maritime Facts and Figures: SHIP RECYCLING Information sources and statistics relating to maritime and shipping INTRODUCTION FLEET CASUALTIES IMO INDUSTRY MARITIME SECURITY PIRACY PORTS NATIONAL / REGIONAL RESEARCH SEAFARERS SHIP RECYCLING TERMINOLOGY Terminology SHIP RECYCLING:  used by IMO and Ministries of Transport/Shipping SHIP DISMANTLING:  used by Basel Convention and Ministries of Environment SHIP BREAKING:  used by International Labour Organization (ILO) and Environmental NGOs DISPOSALS:  used in shipping statistics SCRAPPING:  used by shipowners IMO and UN Agencies IMO The Hong Kong International Convention for the Safe and Environmentally Sound Recycling of Ships, 2009 (the Hong Kong Convention), was adopted at a diplomatic conference held in Hong Kong, China, from 11 to 15 May 2009, which was attended by delegates from 63 countries. Documents from the diplomatic conference are retrievable using the document symbol SR /CONF in the IMO document repository IMODOCS (registration required).  Read more about IMO's work in Ship Recycling here IMO RESOLUTIONS (GUIDELINES) MEPC.196(62) - 2011 GUIDELINES FOR", "http": {"bytes_read": 40839, "content_type": "text/html; charset=UTF-8", "final_url": "https://imo.libguides.com/c.php?g=659460&p=4744890", "redirect_location": null, "requested_at": "2026-11-06T13:39:46.473440+00:00", "response_headers": {}, "sampled_bytes_sha256": "2f1d9a447c46278444d0da19e7ee5098605301357c278ec756b6fcb0f56f92f2", "seconds": 1.081, "status": 200, "truncated": false, "url": "https://imo.libguides.com/c.php?g=659460&p=4744890"}, "id": "imo-guide", "observed_at": "2026-11-06T13:39:36.472997+00:00", "outcome": "captured", "robots_evidence": {"bytes_read": 1090, 